<title>USA: Fed adds reserves via seven-day fixed system RP's.</title>
<headline>Fed adds reserves via seven-day fixed system RP's.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve added temporary reserves to the banking system on Thursday via seven -day fixed system repurchase agreements, a Fed spokesman said.</p>
<p>The Fed's move was in line with the market's expectations.</p>
<p>At 1130 EDT/1530 GMT, the time the Fed usually intervenes in the market, the federal funds rate was quoted at 5-3/16 percent, below the central bank's 5-1/4 percent target.</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1676</p>
</text>
